  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two long parallel conductors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are separated by a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and carrying currents of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> respectively. The conductors are placed along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Y</mi></math> plane. There is a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> located between the conductors (as shown in figure).<br />A charge particle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math> coulomb is passing through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> with velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>; where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> &amp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> represents unit vector along <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;&amp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>axis respectively.<br />The force acting on the charge particle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8096e70b-d3d7-4979-8b96-9a225be55cc4-image.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 203px;\" /></p>",
